course: dictionary
lesson: 5606
title: Words that save lives
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lifesaving is a word made of two smaller words, life and saving. Put them together and the clue is in the word itself: something lifesaving helps to save a life.
explain: «Swimming is great exercise and a lifesaving skill.» The sentence tells you lifesaving is a skill, something you can learn and use. Swap in your meaning, "a skill that can save a person's life", and the sentence still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: Lifesaving can also describe things, like lifesaving medicine. Context tells you which meaning is which: a skill is something a person does, but medicine is a thing that helps a sick person get better.
fact: Lifesaving means able to save someone's life, as in lifesaving medicine.
fact: Lifesaving can also be a noun for the skill of rescuing people from drowning, taught in swimming and lifeguard classes.
fact: Lifesaving skills include CPR and using a defibrillator, which can help a person whose heart has stopped.
fact: Surf Life Saving clubs in Australia and New Zealand teach people how to rescue others at the beach.
fact: You may see it written as «life-saving» with a hyphen; both spellings are correct.
exercise: «Swimming is great exercise and a lifesaving skill.» What does lifesaving mean here? | *A skill that can save a person's life | A way to make swimming cheaper | A kind of fast swimming race | A game played on the beach
exercise: Ella reads about lifesaving medicine. What does lifesaving mean? | Made of soft plastic | *Able to save someone's life | Very tasty | Taken once a year
exercise: Surf Life Saving clubs teach people how to rescue others at the beach. What do these clubs teach? | Sandcastle building | Kite flying | How to cook fish | *How to rescue people
test: «Swimming is great exercise and a lifesaving skill.» Which word tells you lifesaving is something you can learn? | exercise | *skill | swimming | great
test: Lifesaving can mean the skill of rescuing people from drowning. Which two classes teach this skill? | Maths and music | Cooking and art | Dance and reading | *Swimming and lifeguard classes
exam: Jayden reads, «The defibrillator is a lifesaving machine.» What does lifesaving most likely mean? | Only for the summer | *Able to save a person's life | Very noisy | Painted bright red
